---
const skills = ['AI-assisted design', 'Prompt engineering', 'Design-to-code', 'Design systems'];
---

<section id="about" class="section bg-white about-section">
  <div class="container space-y-20">

    <!-- About heading + two-col bio -->
    <div>
      <div class="border-t border-gray-200 mb-4"></div>
      <h2 class="font-medium text-black mb-12" style="font-size: 56px; letter-spacing: -2.2px; line-height: 67.2px;">About</h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
        <!-- Left: intro -->
        <div class="space-y-6" style="font-size: 24px; letter-spacing: -0.7px; line-height: 1.45; color: rgba(0,0,0,0.659);">
          <p>
            I'm Zehra - a product designer who doesn't just design interfaces, I build them.
          </p>
          <p>
            Over the past few years I've turned complex problems into experiences people actually enjoy using - and lately, I've been closing the gap between design and code myself, using AI as a real collaborator, not a shortcut. Currently designing and building from Mostar, Bosnia and Herzegovina.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: detail paragraphs -->
        <div class="space-y-5" style="font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.4px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(0,0,0,0.549);">
          <p>
            I'm currently a <span class="text-black font-medium">Senior Product Designer at Fitify</span>, designing core experiences for an AI-powered fitness and nutrition platform used by casual fitness enthusiasts worldwide. My work spans workout flows, calorie tracking, onboarding, and A/B experimentation - always grounded in user behavior and retention data.
          </p>
          <p>
            Outside my day-to-day, I design with AI, not just around it. I use Claude Code, Cursor, and v0 to take my own concepts from idea to deployed product - building tools like an AI brief generator and a Spotify playlist cover generator, end to end, and a lot more. I treat prompt engineering as a design skill, and I use Figma's MCP integration to keep design systems and code in sync rather than in two separate worlds.
          </p>
          <p>
            Previously, I worked at <span class="text-black font-medium">Rolla</span>, a fast-growing health-tech startup, where I built the Health module from scratch and redesigned the Rolla Diet module. Before that, I worked with early-stage startups at SixBerries (UK), turning founders' ideas into real, shipped products across health, edtech, and fintech.
          </p>
          <p>
            I believe AI raises the floor for what one designer can ship - but the judgment, the taste, and the "why" behind every decision are still entirely human. That's the space I work in.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Skills -->
    <div>
      <div class="border-t border-gray-200 mb-4"></div>
      <h2 class="font-medium text-black mb-10" style="font-size: 56px; letter-spacing: -2.2px; line-height: 67.2px;">Skills</h2>
      <div class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
        {skills.map((skill) => (
          <p class="font-medium text-black py-6" style="font-size: 80px; letter-spacing: -4px; line-height: 1.05;">
            {skill}
          </p>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-section .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
    }
    .about-section h2 {
      font-size: 40px !important;
      letter-spacing: -1.5px !important;
      line-height: 1.2 !important;
      margin-bottom: 24px !important;
    }
    .about-section p[style*="font-size: 24px"] {
      font-size: 18px !important;
    }
    .about-section p[style*="font-size: 80px"] {
      font-size: 36px !important;
      letter-spacing: -2px !important;
      padding-top: 16px !important;
      padding-bottom: 16px !important;
    }
  }
</style>
